{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the progression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/39939068ede0c2079b01c4d63e91db8bd589a973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{\\dfrac{1}{11}}, 10^{\\dfrac{2}{11}}, 10^{\\dfrac{3}{11}}, 10^{\\dfrac{4}{11}},\\dots , 10^{\\dfrac{n}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"268\" height=\"42\" />. \nThe least positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that the product of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms of the progression exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d545bb45d1f0199e4785046df6c11481c9164de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f273e545647a583c28cbcb8fda71b158e56108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }7\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }8\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }9\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }10\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"370\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the rules of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Exponentiation\" title=\"Exponentiation\">exponents</a>, the product of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms of the sequence equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030d4575afe7510a52711eaf6c6b1f6b78d32ddc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{\\frac{1}{11}+\\frac{2}{11}+\\dots+\\frac{n}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />. From here, we can set up the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/91422ec11caee17e5f5d3dd837ba51d2a98228d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{\\frac{1}{11}+\\frac{2}{11}+\\dots+\\frac{n}{11}}=100,000=10^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"23\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0017a1389050486899b2f3fdd7f74f9d25bfbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{11}+\\frac{2}{11}+\\dots+\\frac{n}{11}=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd30e12e84a8c2cda8098754aad554c0188e77a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3\\dots n=55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"151\" height=\"14\" />. By the formula for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangular_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangular numbers\">triangular numbers</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e915dbeccb981d301ed04ba3b50bb46055ac18c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}=55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"40\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e69736cd301524668306fcb06f7e1a46c06d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+n-110=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc83e1360dacd66be6fd8ebba3df59ecd2727ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+11)(n-10)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0247db3d702b5ce6be98f50771750a2723cddcea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1b21210db29332b1a7d9ce088fd457f23aeee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> makes the product equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d545bb45d1f0199e4785046df6c11481c9164de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />. However, we have to strictly exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d545bb45d1f0199e4785046df6c11481c9164de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/6379e57883418fb3da3018d5eab910e5553fe535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"66\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1971 A